 "round": "The Great Work",
 "intro": "The alchemist's notebook was written so that only a fellow adept could read it. Every page is a different recipe, and every recipe is a lie with one true ingredient. In the west corner of the laboratory stands the old sorting rack, its shallow shelves cut one by one to cradle each vessel exactly as it finds them, no two alike, no one shared. The novices are forbidden to touch it; the masters add to it in silence, setting down the day's yield where it naturally falls. A visitor once asked why the shelves were made so oddly, and the old master only smiled and said that everything in the Work has its proper place.",
 "echo": "Everything that matters here was tested in fire, and Arthur Miller named a play after the vessel.",
